.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt PLAKAR-NOTION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm plakar-notion
.Nd Plakar integration to back up and restore Notion pages and databases
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
integration backs up the pages and databases a Notion workspace shares
with an internal integration, and restores them under a page of a
workspace, through the Notion API.
.Pp
Pages and databases are stored as the API returns them, as JSON, one
directory per object named by its id.
The blocks of a page are stored in one file with their children nested,
and the files Notion hosts for a page, images or PDFs say, are stored
next to it.
.Sh REQUIREMENTS
An internal integration and its secret, created at
.Lk https://www.notion.so/profile/integrations .
The integration must be connected to each top-level page or database
to back up or restore under; everything below a connected page is
reachable.
Backing up needs the
.Dq Read content
capability, restoring also needs
.Dq Insert content .
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Bl -tag -width skip_attachments
.It Ar location
For a backup,
.Li notion://
backs up everything shared with the integration, and
.Li notion://<id>
one page or database and what is under it.
For a restore, the id of the page to restore under; the API cannot
create pages at the top of a workspace.
A pasted Notion URL is accepted in place of an id.
.It Ar token
The integration secret, starting with
.Li ntn_ .
.It Ar skip_attachments
Leave out the files Notion hosts.
Off by default.
.El
.Sh USAGE
Back up a workspace:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar source add notes notion:// token=ntn_xxx
$ plakar at /var/backups/plakar backup @notes
.Ed
.Pp
Restore a snapshot under a page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar destination add notes-restore notion://<page-id> token=ntn_xxx
$ plakar at /var/backups/plakar restore -to @notes-restore <snapshot>
.Ed
.Sh CAVEATS
A restore always creates new pages; the API cannot put a page back under
its old id.
What the API cannot recreate is reported on the record it belonged to
and the rest is restored: unsupported, link preview and template blocks,
rollup, status and unique id properties, relations to a database that is
not in the restore, computed values, comments, hosted files larger
than 20 MB, and hosted files held in a
.Dq files
property.
A page that lived under a block is created under its page instead.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr plakar 1 ,
.Xr plakar-backup 1 ,
.Xr plakar-restore 1 ,
.Lk https://developers.notion.com/reference
